IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `whs-claims-seat`

-- Cases for whs-claims-seat.l4. Every expected value was worked by hand from the text of the Act (Compilation No. 16),
-- before the encoding was run. Dates are `the date` day month year. All cases are hypothetical.

§ `Cases -- a claimant under the Work Health and Safety Act 2011`

§§ `s 105 -- discriminatory conduct`

#ASSERT `Is what was done to me discriminatory conduct?` `dismissed me (s 105(1)(a)(i))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what was done to me discriminatory conduct?` `altered my position to my detriment (s 105(1)(a)(iv))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what was done to me discriminatory conduct?` `offered me worse terms of engagement than another prospective worker (s 105(1)(b)(ii))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what was done to me discriminatory conduct?` `refused or failed to enter into a commercial arrangement with me (s 105(1)(d))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is what was done to me discriminatory conduct?` `none of these` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 106 -- prohibited reason`

#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason?` `I am, was or proposed to be a health and safety representative or committee member (s 106(a))` `I did not raise an issue` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason?` `I exercised, or proposed to exercise, a power under the Act, such as stopping unsafe work (s 106(d))` `I did not raise an issue` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason?` `I raised, or proposed to raise, a health or safety issue or concern (s 106(h))` `an inspector (s 106(h)(ii))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason?` `I raised, or proposed to raise, a health or safety issue or concern (s 106(h))` `another worker (s 106(h)(vi))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (h) closes its list: raising it only with the media or family is not a prohibited reason under (h).
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason?` `I raised, or proposed to raise, a health or safety issue or concern (s 106(h))` `someone else, such as the media, a family member or a friend` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason?` `I raised, or proposed to raise, a health or safety issue or concern (s 106(h))` `I did not raise an issue` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it done for a prohibited reason?` `another reason` `the business or undertaking (s 106(h)(i))` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 108 -- coercion or inducement`

#ASSERT `Was I coerced or induced?` TRUE TRUE `give up seeking, or stop holding, a role under the Act (s 108(1)(d))` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I coerced or induced?` TRUE TRUE `use, or not use, a power under the Act (s 108(1)(a))` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I coerced or induced?` TRUE TRUE `something else` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I coerced or induced?` TRUE FALSE `use, or not use, a power under the Act (s 108(1)(a))` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I coerced or induced?` FALSE TRUE `use, or not use, a power under the Act (s 108(1)(a))` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I coerced or induced?` TRUE TRUE `use, or not use, a power under the Act (s 108(1)(a))` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 109 -- misrepresentation`

#ASSERT `Was I misled about my rights?` TRUE TRUE `my rights or obligations under the Act (s 109(1)(a))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I misled about my rights?` TRUE TRUE `whether I can complain or inquire to someone who enforces the Act (s 109(1)(c))` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I misled about my rights?` TRUE TRUE `my rights or obligations under the Act (s 109(1)(a))` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I misled about my rights?` TRUE FALSE `my rights or obligations under the Act (s 109(1)(a))` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was I misled about my rights?` TRUE TRUE `something else` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 112, 113(1), 115 -- starting a court proceeding`

-- Knew on 15 March 2026: the last day is 15 March 2027.
#ASSERT `By what day must I start?` (`the date` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `the date` 15 3 2027
-- 29 February 2024: one year on is read as 28 February 2025 (fork F4).
#ASSERT `By what day must I start?` (`the date` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `the date` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `Can I start a court proceeding?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `the person affected (s 112(6)(a))` (`the date` 15 3 2026) (`the date` 15 3 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I may apply to a court for an order under s 112 (s 112(1)), in the Federal Court, the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2) or a Supreme Court (s 273A)`
#ASSERT `Can I start a court proceeding?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `the person affected (s 112(6)(a))` (`the date` 15 3 2026) (`the date` 16 3 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it is more than 1 year after I knew or ought to have known of the claim (s 113(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I start a court proceeding?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `the person affected (s 112(6)(a))` (`the date` 29 2 2024) (`the date` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it is more than 1 year after I knew or ought to have known of the claim (s 113(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I start a court proceeding?` `coercion or inducement under s 108` `a representative authorised by the person affected (s 112(6)(b))` (`the date` 15 3 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I may apply to a court for an order under s 112 (s 112(1)), in the Federal Court, the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2) or a Supreme Court (s 273A)`
#ASSERT `Can I start a court proceeding?` `misrepresentation under s 109` `the person affected (s 112(6)(a))` (`the date` 15 3 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: nothing I complain of is conduct s 112(2) reaches (misrepresentation under s 109 is an offence only)`
#ASSERT `Can I start a court proceeding?` `nothing Part 6 prohibits` `the person affected (s 112(6)(a))` (`the date` 15 3 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: nothing I complain of is conduct s 112(2) reaches (misrepresentation under s 109 is an offence only)`
#ASSERT `Can I start a court proceeding?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `someone else` (`the date` 15 3 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am not an eligible person (s 112(6))`
#ASSERT `Can I start a court proceeding?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `the person affected (s 112(6)(a))` (`the date` 15 3 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: I have another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter that is not withdrawn (s 115(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I start a court proceeding?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `the person affected (s 112(6)(a))` (`the date` 15 3 2026) (`the date` 1 6 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: I failed in another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter, not a workers' compensation one (s 115(c))`

§§ `ss 112(3), 113(2), (3), 114(3), 115(b) -- the orders`

#ASSERT `What orders can the court make for me?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `an injunction (s 112(3)(a))`, `compensation within a specified period (s 112(3)(b))`, `reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position applied for (s 112(3)(c))`, `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112(3)(d))`
#ASSERT `What orders can the court make for me?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `an injunction (s 112(3)(a))`, `compensation within a specified period (s 112(3)(b))`, `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112(3)(d))`
#ASSERT `What orders can the court make for me?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `they requested, instructed, induced, encouraged, authorised or assisted another to do it (s 112(2)(b))` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `an injunction (s 112(3)(a))`, `compensation within a specified period (s 112(3)(b))`, `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112(3)(d))`
#ASSERT `What orders can the court make for me?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS LIST `an injunction (s 112(3)(a))`, `reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position applied for (s 112(3)(c))`, `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112(3)(d))`
#ASSERT `What orders can the court make for me?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `What orders can the court make for me?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `What orders can the court make for me?` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
-- Coercion: no presumption, no defence, no compensation, no reinstatement; an injunction or another order only.
#ASSERT `What orders can the court make for me?` `coercion or inducement under s 108` `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `an injunction (s 112(3)(a))`, `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112(3)(d))`
#ASSERT `What orders can the court make for me?` `misrepresentation under s 109` `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `What orders can the court make for me?` `nothing Part 6 prohibits` `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `ss 104(2), 110, 111, 114(2) -- the criminal side`

#ASSERT `Can they be convicted for discriminating against me?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they be convicted for discriminating against me?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can they be convicted for discriminating against me?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `What orders can a criminal court make for me?` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `compensation within a specified period, on conviction (s 111(a))`, `reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position applied for, on conviction (s 111(b))`
#ASSERT `What orders can a criminal court make for me?` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `compensation within a specified period, on conviction (s 111(a))`
#ASSERT `What orders can a criminal court make for me?` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `What orders can a criminal court make for me?` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `What is the most they can be fined for it?` FALSE EQUALS 139000
#ASSERT `What is the most they can be fined for it?` TRUE EQUALS 695000

